LassoCssLexer incorrectly identified as best match for C code

#### Description

The LassoCssLexer is being incorrectly selected when analyzing C code, causing wrong syntax highlighting. This appears to be related to the lexer's `analyse_text` method returning unexpectedly high confidence scores.

#### Steps/Code to Reproduce

```python
from pygments.lexers import guess_lexer

code = '''
    #include <stdio.h>
    #include <stdlib.h>

    int main(void);

    int main(void) {
        uint8_t x = 42;
        uint8_t y = x + 1;

        /* exit 1 for success! */
        return 1;
    }
    '''

lexer = guess_lexer(code)
print(lexer.__class__.__name__)  # Expected: CLexer, Actual: LassoCssLexer
```

The lexer detection is also failing when using the command line interface:

```bash
echo "x" | pygmentize -C
```

Expected output: `text`
Actual output: `lasso+css`

This affects proper syntax highlighting of C code and other simple text content.
